-- title:
--   Kernel tuple fixed iff the cyclic subgroup is preserved
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $(M' : \kappa) \neq 0$, and let $W$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$. Let $T$ assign to each prime factor $p$ of $M'$ a polynomial $T_p \in \kappa[X]$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) $W$ $p$ $k_p$ $T_p$, where $k_p = v_p(M')$: when $p^{k_p} = 2$ this says $\deg T_p \le 1$, the coefficient of $X$ in $T_p$ is $1$ and $T_p \mid W.\Psi_2^{\,2}$; otherwise it says $\deg T_p \le \varphi(p^{k_p})/2$, the coefficient of $X^{\varphi(p^{k_p})/2}$ is $1$, $T_p \cdot W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p^{k_p-1}) \mid W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p^{k_p})$, and $T_p \mid W.\mathrm{smulNumerator}\,a\,(\varphi(p^{k_p})/2)\,T_p$ for all $a$ with $2 \le a \le (p^{k_p}-1)/2$ and $p \nmid a$. Let $g$ be an affine point of exact order $M'$, linked to $T$ in the sense that whenever $n \cdot g$ is an affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ of exact order $p^{k_p}$, the abscissa $x_1$ is a root of $T_p$. Let $C$ be a Weierstrass variable change with $C \bullet W = W$. Then the tuple $T$ is fixed by $C$, i.e. $u^{-2 d_p} T_p(u^2 X + r) = T_p$ for every prime factor $p$, where $u, r$ are the corresponding data of $C$ and $d_p = 1$ if $p^{k_p} = 2$ and $d_p = \varphi(p^{k_p})/2$ otherwise, if and only if the point transport [`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.equivOfVariableChangeEq hC`](def/WeierstrassCurve_VariableChangePointEquiv.html#L152) maps the set of integer multiples of $g$ onto itself.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the polynomial and the group-theoretic descriptions of a $\Gamma_0(M')$-type level structure on a fixed Weierstrass model: a change of variables preserving the model fixes the tuple of generator-kernel polynomials exactly when the induced automorphism of the group of points preserves the cyclic subgroup generated by $g$. It feeds the comparison of cardinalities in [`ModularCurve.natCard_variableChange_smul_eq_and_kernelVariableChangeDeg_eq_eq_natCard_rationalAut_map_zmultiples_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.natCard_variableChange_smul_eq_and_kernelVariableChangeDeg_eq_eq_natCard_rationalAut_map_zmultiples_eq).
